        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Kluge, Sidney Salkow, Kay Harris, William Tracy, George Watts\n- Films: Yesterday Girl, Tillie the Toiler\n- Topics: New German Cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Salkow was born on June 16, 1911, and died on October 18, 2000.\n- Alexander Kluge was born on 14 February 1932.\n- Tillie the Toiler is a 1941 American comedy film directed by Sidney Salkow and starring Kay Harris, William Tracy, and George Watts.\n- Yesterday Girl is a 1966 New German Cinema film directed and written by Alexander Kluge.\n- Alexander Kluge is a German author, philosopher, academic, and film director.\n- Sidney Salkow was an American film director, screenwriter, and television director, and he directed more than 50 motion pictures.",
